<div class="table-wrap">
<table class="observations">
  <caption>Every answer we recorded for this claim. One row per answer; personas are never averaged.</caption>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th scope="col">Chatbot</th>
      <th scope="col">Country</th>
      <th scope="col">Language</th>
      <th scope="col">Persona</th>
      <th scope="col">Date</th>
      <th scope="col">Model version</th>
      <th scope="col">Behaviour</th>
      <th scope="col">Kremlin-linked domains cited</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for observation in claim.observations %}
    <tr>
      <th scope="row">{{ observation.chatbot | chatbotLabel }}</th>
      <td>{{ observation.country | countryName }}</td>
      <td>{{ observation.language | languageName }}</td>
      <td data-persona="{{ observation.persona }}">{{ observation.persona }}</td>
      <td><time datetime="{{ observation.date | isoDate }}">{{ observation.date | displayDate }}</time></td>
      <td>{{ observation.model_version | default("not reported") }}</td>
      <td><span class="badge badge-{{ observation.behaviour }}">{{ observation.behaviour | behaviourLabel }}</span></td>
      <td>{% if observation.cited_domains | length %}{% for domain in observation.cited_domains %}<span class="domain">{{ domain | defang }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}{% else %}none{% endif %}</td>
    </tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p class="note">Personas are four ways of asking the same question, from a neutral check to a request to write the narrative. Each row is one answer under one persona; we do not average across them, because a model can hold under a neutral question and give way under a leading one.</p>
